<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    No Slack client library, deliberately, and this is a decision rather than an omission.

    The ingress needs four things: prove the request came from Slack, deduplicate a retry,
    normalise an event into a ChatMessage, and carry the bounded shapes those produce. All four
    are a few hundred lines over System.Text.Json, they are tested, and a client library would be
    a large dependency doing none of them.

    SlackNet earns its place when this system needs to CALL the Slack Web API: posting a warning,
    deleting a message, restricting an account. That is the interventions plan, and the dependency
    should be added there, against the calls that need it.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\StyloMail.Core\StyloMail.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
